\section{Sequence numbering}{

Sequences are read from the assay object: \verb{$assay$as_ref}, \verb{$assay$as_alt},
\verb{$assay$com} and the amplicon.  The amplicon is taken from
\verb{$assay$amplicon_seq} when present; otherwise it is sliced from
\verb{$template$seq} between the outer primer coordinates and, for an assay on the
minus strand, reverse-complemented so every sequence is listed 5' to 3' in
the orientation of its assay.  Degenerate (IUPAC) primers cannot be listed
unambiguously and abort with the offending role.
}

\section{Sequence listing schema}{

WIPO publishes the ST.26 schema; it does not ship with this package (external
data never ships).  Put \code{ST26SequenceListing_V1_3.xsd} in the per-user cache
directory, \code{tools::R_user_dir("tidymarkers", "cache")} (see
\code{\link[=marker_cache_dir]{marker_cache_dir()}}), then validation runs automatically on export and on
demand with \code{\link[=marker_patent_validate]{marker_patent_validate()}}.  The standards page is
\url{https://www.wipo.int/standards/en/}; the exact archive URL is supplied by the
operator, and the one-line install is
\verb{curl -L -o "<cache>/ST26SequenceListing_V1_3.xsd" "<WIPO ST.26 XSD URL>"}.
Without the XSD the XML is still written, with a warning that it was not
validated.
